  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Chef has two integers AAA and BBB. In one operation he can choose any integer d,d,d, and make one of the following two moves :\n\n\nAdd ddd to AAA and subtract ddd from BBB.\nAdd ddd to BBB and subtract ddd from AAA.\nChef is allowed to make as many operations as he wants. Can he make AAA and BBB **equal**?\n\n\nInput Format\n\nFirst line will contain TTT, number of test cases. Then the test cases follow.\nEach test case contains of a single line of input, two integers A,BA, BA,B.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, if Chef can make the two numbers equal print `YES` else print `NO`.\n\n\nYou may print each character of the string in uppercase or lowercase (for example, the strings `yEs`, `Yes`, `YeS`, and `YES` will all be treated as identical).",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤10001 \\leq T \\leq 10001≤T≤1000",
      "1≤A,B≤10001 \\leq A,B \\leq 10001≤A,B≤1000"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "2\n3 3\n1 2",
        "output": "Yes\nNo",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: Since AAA and BBB are already equal, Chef does not need any operations.\nTest case 222: It can be shown that AAA and BBB can never be made equal using any number of given operations."
      }
    ]
  },
